# CODEOWNERS example - for teams (not needed for solo projects).
#
# What it does: automatically requests a review from the right person/team when
# a PR touches files they own, and (with branch protection) requires their
# approval before merge. This is how larger/cross-team review scales without a
# central bottleneck.
#
# To use: save as .github/CODEOWNERS (or CODEOWNERS at repo root).
# Syntax: <path pattern>   <@user or @org/team>
# Later matches win, so put general rules first and specific rules last.
#
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default owner for everything (fallback)
*                           @uicacer/rse-team

# Data pipeline / anything touching PHI - require the security champion too
/pipelines/                 @uicacer/rse-team @the-security-champion
/healthlake/                @uicacer/rse-team @the-security-champion
/**/fhir_mapping/           @uicacer/rse-team @the-security-champion

# ML / model code
/models/                    @the-ml-lead

# Infrastructure (AWS, CI config) - higher-stakes, require infra owner
/infrastructure/            @the-infra-owner
/.github/workflows/         @the-infra-owner

# Docs can be owned more loosely
/docs/                      @uicacer/rse-team
